    "updated_at": "2022-05-12T15:16:20Z",
    "body": "Having thought more about this, I realized that the behavior of `random_classical_hamiltonian` is expected. Since the function necessarily creates a random hamiltonian, it may or may not contain terms containing all qubits in the specified register. \r\nTo avoid getting errors like above, users or any defined workflows should carefully set the register of mixer Hamiltonian to match that of Cost Hamiltonian constructed using `random_classical_hamiltonian`",
